## 6. Methods & Identification Strategy

**Estimators / models**
Data will be analyses through Difference-in-difference analysis (H1), and panel fixed-effects regression (H2).

**Identification strategy.** 
In order to prevent overstating the causality of AI's proposed impacts on fraud detection, Overall audit fees as well as the ratio of audit fees to total fees
will be used to mediate for the differences seen between companies of differing sizes and companies with differing levels of focus on auditing.

**Validation & robustness**
Cross-validation will be used to split the data into 5 folds as a means of testing robustness of the results.


## 7. Analysis Plan & Expected Outcomes

**Pre-specified analyses:**
*Logistical Regression*
As the DV of focus (Fraud detection) is binary in nature (Detected/Not Detected),
an analysis that measures the changes in probability of one outcome occuring over the other is the method to use.

**What supports vs. refutes each hypothesis**

| Hypothesis | Supported if… | Refuted if… |
|---|---|---|
| H1 | Logistical Regression presents a p-value <0.05 regarding whether fraud detection is different when year <2023| p-value regarding year>=0.05 |
| H2 | Logistical Regression presents a p-value <0.05 regarding whether fraud detection is different between term and reason polarities on sentences mentioning AI | p-value regarding sentence >=0.05 |

